{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "Neoclassical combining forms",
    "language": "mul",
    "description": "Greek and Latin combining forms, shared across languages rather than belonging to any one of them. hypo + therm yields English hypothermic, Spanish hipotermia and French hypothermie from the same two morphemes. That is why this file sits in shared/ and not under en/: a learner who owns these morphemes owns vocabulary in every language that borrowed them, which is the cognate bridge first-language instruction depends on.",
    "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
    "credits": "../CREDITS.md",
    "status": "seed+ - the common science set. Greek/Latin combining forms are open-ended; origins/positions on the 2026-07-22 assistant batch are unreviewed.",
    "_short_form_caveat": "Forms of one or two letters (di, bi, an, tri, eu) match the start of many unrelated words. A consumer must not split on them unless the REMAINDER is itself a listed morpheme or word - the same corner-is-not-corn-plus-er guard the base-morpheme inventory uses. Position alone is not enough here."
  },
  "_provenance": {
    "_note": "Who added what, when, and how. Recorded per BATCH rather than per entry: the data was created in batches, so batch records are honest and stay readable, while an entry needing individual sourcing (a teacher contribution, a single corrected form) may carry its own `prov` field.\n\nBatches are identified by DATE and COMMIT SUBJECT, deliberately not by commit hash. A hash means nothing to a human auditor and breaks the moment history is ever rewritten; a subject line is stable, readable, and findable with `git log --grep`.\n\n`method` is the load-bearing field. `authored` = compiled from facts by a person. `mined` = derived by code from a corpus named in PROVENANCE.md. `assistant` = drafted by an AI assistant at the maintainer's direction and accepted by the maintainer. All three produce uncopyrightable facts, so none affects the free-forever promise; recording which is which lets a downstream user filter and keeps the chain auditable by someone who was not here.",
    "batches": [
      {
        "date": "2026-07-22",
        "commit_subject": "data: neoclassical combining forms, and Class I/II levels on the suffixes",
        "method": "assistant",
        "scope": "combiningForms (9 neoclassical forms with position); -ic/-al/-ous added to derivational suffixes; Class I/II `level` field",
        "by": "AI assistant, directed and accepted by the maintainer"
      },
      {
        "date": "2026-07-22",
        "commit_subject": "shared: expand science combining forms",
        "method": "assistant",
        "by": "AI assistant, directed by the maintainer; ORIGINS AND POSITIONS NOT YET REVIEWED - drafted from general knowledge of Greek/Latin roots and expected to contain errors until a maintainer or linguist checks them",
        "scope": "+89 Greek/Latin combining forms common in science vocabulary: SI prefixes (kilo/centi/milli/nano), quantity (mono/di/tri/poly), spatial (endo/exo/trans), roots (bio/geo/hydro/electro/cyto) and final forms (-lysis/-sphere/-troph/-vore/-gen); +pro (forward), potent (power/able), kine (movement) added same session; mot (move)",
        "prompted_by": "morphology-into-science-vocabulary line - Trussell et al. 2018; the combining-form layer is what that instruction operationalises (endo+thermic, hydro+lysis, photo+synthesis)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "_note": "Neoclassical combining forms, from Greek and Latin. They belong in neither existing list: not `bases`, because they are not free words (there is no word 'therm'), and not `prefixes`, because prefixes attach to a free base while these combine with EACH OTHER - hypo+therm+ic has no free word anywhere in it. This is the layer that connects concepts rather than parses sentences: hypothermic and hyperthermic share `therm` and contrast only on hypo/hyper, and a learner who owns those three morphemes owns both words plus thermometer, thermal and isotherm.",
  "_position": "Position is not free. An initial form precedes a final one, and most are fixed to one slot: photo- and hypo- are initial, -logy and -meter final, while therm and graph occur in both. Recorded per entry rather than assumed, because a parser that tries every form in every slot will split words that should stay whole.",
